# Keep secrets OUT of the image. `COPY . .` would otherwise bake .env and any
# OAuth token files into a layer, where they survive even if a later layer
# deletes them and travel with the image anywhere it is pushed. Render injects
# configuration as environment variables instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
*credentials*.json
*token*.json

# Local-only state and build noise - none of it belongs in a container, and
# excluding it keeps the build context (and image) small.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.git/
.gitignore
.adk/
app/.adk/
.work/
node_modules/

# Docs and design sources the runtime never reads. Listed explicitly rather
# than as a blanket *.md: skills/*.md and skills/agents/*.md ARE runtime inputs
# (app.config.agent_instructions / load_skill read them at agent-build time),
# and excluding them would silently fall back to inline default prompts.
architecture/
docs/
README.md

# Editor / OS noise
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
